What the MIT license covers
---------------------------

The MIT license in LICENSE covers the source code in this repository: the
planner, the stat engine, the schema, the extractor, the build tools, and the
Forge exporter mod under mod/.

It does not cover game data or art belonging to anyone else. Specifically:

  * Registry data, stat values and textures extracted from a Craft to Exile 2
    install remain the property of their respective authors. Mine and Slash is
    by robertx22; Craft to Exile 2 is by the CTE team.

  * The `site-data` branch of this repository carries a copy of that data and
    those textures so the GitHub Pages build has something to load. They are not
    licensed to you under LICENSE, and nothing here grants you any right in them:
    forking the planner does not carry a right to redistribute the art.

  * The `main` branch contains no extracted game data at all, and the desktop
    app redistributes none — it reads from the install on the machine it runs
    on. See .gitignore.

No Mine and Slash, Library of Exile or Minecraft code is included or vendored
here. The exporter mod under mod/ compiles against those jars with `compileOnly`
and never bundles them.


Third-party components
----------------------

Nothing is vendored into this repository; the build resolves its dependencies
from npm. The packaged desktop application additionally bundles Electron, which
carries Chromium, Node.js and V8. Their licenses ship inside the packaged
application, as produced by electron-builder.
